---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Subscribe from '../components/Subscribe.astro';
import Trajectory from '../components/Trajectory.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

---
<Base title="About" description="How Lalit Shewani went from software engineer to senior AI product manager, across JP Morgan Chase and Ford.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1 class="h1">A bit about me</h1>
      <p class="lead">I have spent 8+ years across product and engineering, most of it inside large, regulated enterprises.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="story-flow wide"><Trajectory /></div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h3">Where it started</h2>
      <p>I joined JP Morgan Chase in 2018 as a software engineer. I built Java services for trade processing and helped move old C++ systems to a modern Java architecture.</p>
      <p>In 2021 I moved to the product side of a data platform. I spent those years replacing batch exports with stream-based delivery and getting five engineering pods to agree on how new data should come in.</p>

      <h2 class="h3">Moving into AI</h2>
      <p>From 2023 I was a technical product manager. I owned the roadmap for a trade-processing platform, and I shipped machine learning products: predictive anomaly detection and a self-service LLM assistant for analysts.</p>
      <p>In June 2026 I joined Ford’s AI Advancement Center as a senior product manager. I work on document intelligence, an audit system where a person always signs off, and a retrieval platform for teams outside engineering.</p>

      <h2 class="h3">What I pay attention to</h2>
      <p>I trained as an engineer, so I stay close to evals and retrieval quality. The question I keep coming back to is simpler, though: does the person using it trust it enough to use it again tomorrow?</p>

      <h2 class="h3">Outside the day job</h2>
      <p>At JP Morgan Chase I founded the Bengaluru product management community events, ProdCon and Prodathon, and coached four associate PMs. I also wrote a newsletter on the technology behind investment banking.</p>
      <p>This site is where I keep writing. The <a href="/lessons/">product lessons</a> come from the work, and the <a href="/builds/">late-night builds</a> are what I make outside it.</p>

      <h2 class="h3">Education</h2>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>B.E. in Electronics and Electrical Engineering, minor in Finance, BITS Pilani, Goa Campus</li>
        <li>Executive Certificate in Product Management, Indian School of Business</li>
        <li>AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a class="btn" href={site.resume} download>Download resume</a></p>
    </div>

    {site.photo && (
      <figure class="portrait">
        <img src={site.photoLarge} alt="Lalit Shewani, arms folded, looking to the side" loading="lazy" width="480" height="480" />
      </figure>
    )}

    <div class="block"><Subscribe /></div>
  </div>
</Base>
